Package: python3-qemu-tool
Architecture: all
Depends: ${python3:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: CLI tool for running and generating QEMU VMs
 qemu-tool provides two subcommands: run-vm launches a QEMU virtual machine
 with a flexible set of options for networking, storage, PCI passthrough, and
 architecture (amd64, arm64, riscv64); gen-vm creates a new cloud-init-seeded
 VM image using debootstrap or a cloud image download.
 .
 VM images are stored in /var/lib/qemu-tool/images (kvm group writable).
